# Jaguar Mark 1 2.4 Litre four-door saloon, 1955-1959.
#
# The compact Jaguar that created the sports-saloon class: a unitary body with
# a sharp rear roofline, small tail fins, a split grille with a central chrome
# bar and a curved chrome bumper. The 2.4 is the first version; the 3.4 of 1957
# shares the shell.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_Mark_1
#
# Dimensions 4.60 x 1.70 x 1.45 m, wheelbase 2.73 m.
#
# Shape reference: no true level side elevation and no rear view exist in the
# pack. The best are a near-side about 30 degrees off, a front three-quarter and
# a front detail; the flank and tail are reconciled within the published
# dimensions. Only one image is documented as a 2.4. The limitations are
# recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK brochure was consulted. British Racing Green,
# Black, Pearl Grey and Carmen Red are period Jaguar finishes. Weights 7, 6, 4,
# 3, total 20, reflecting the model's volume, provisional pending the central
# rebase.
#
# Speed 160 km/h. Comfort 70/435, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 70. Classes 2,3.
# Dates 1955-1959 production, road tail staggered 1972-1974.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-mk1-24.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-mk1-24.dae. References:
# citycars/references/jaguar-mk1-24/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: no true side elevation and no rear view exist; the best
# is a near-side about 30 degrees off, with a front three-quarter and a front
# detail. The flank and tail are reconciled within the published dimensions.
# Only one image is documented as a 2.4.


